==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Acarodermatitis Hand.jpg|thumb|scabies of the hand]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|scabies|scabiēs|scurf; scab, mange, itch|lang=la}}, from {{term|scabo|scabō|scratch, scrape|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈskei.biz/}}
* {{rhymes|eɪbiz}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{context|pathology}} An infestation of parasitic [[mite]]s, ''Sarcoptes scabiei'', causing intense itching caused by the mites burrowing into the skin of humans and other animals. It is easily transmissible from human to human; secondary skin infection may occur.

====Related terms====
* [[scab]]

